   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/activity-7505176847345946624-I_Hi",
   "text": "A quantitative explanation for why NVIDIA's P/E multiples may be compressed. \n\nNVIDIA's(and GPUs like AMD/Intel) dominance in AI training is unquestionable. This is because AI model training is heavy on matrix multiplications (FLOPs) and NVIDIA has a CUDA moat on training. I expect the same dominance to continue in the next few years too. \n\nBut the problem is that compute workload is of two kinds: TRAINING and INFERENCE. The share of TRAINING as a proportion of total compute workload has gradually been going down in the last few quarters. \nTo give an analogy, model TRAINING is when the AI model(Like ChatGPT) learns how to be smart, and TRAINING is like the AI giving an exam where we humans a",
